From a85c0b4e4091566880821c94fe2325078b1ea81c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 150/150] XD Netplay v1.7.2: Watch only spectators; only the
 opponent can submit a team

A joiner can tick Watch only. The server seats the joiner who is not
watching and has waited longest as the opponent (GBA 2), and every room
shows each player as Host, Opponent, Waiting or Watching. Start maps GBA 2
to that player instead of pid 2, and refuses when nobody is seated.

Only the opponent's TeamData is written; anyone else gets a private
refusal. When the seat changes hands, the previous player's team and model
are cleared before the new opponent's submission or at Start. A Start and a
team write can no longer overlap, and a team sent while the last battle is
still closing is refused instead of lost.

Watchers see no GBA screen, are left out of the lobby player count and the
automatic buffer. Server chat lines no longer add a blank player row or a
false "Not all players have the game" prompt, the host sees each team
line once, and the Use my save note now says that everyone in the room
receives the party.
